# cytosine.msf
# Cytosine (4-aminopyrimidin-2(1H)-one)
# pKa1=4.600 (cytosinium N3+ → cytosine, q=+1→0)
# pKa2=12.160 (cytosine N1-H → cytosinate, q=0→-1)
# Source: Perrin 1981
# First pyrimidine nucleobase in training set (adenine is a purine).
# Two distinct ionisation steps: aromatic N-base (step1) and lactam N-H
# (step2). Step2 is a new LFER key — high-pKa N-H in an aromatic lactam.
# Direct relevance for DNA/RNA protonation state modelling.

[microstate]
